--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS CASE HAD TO ANSWER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
"IPv4_BFD - With RIP v1/v2" asks whether BFD can be bound to RIP so that RIP
reacts to a BFD failure detection instead of to its own 180 s timeout. Three
things had to be separated, because a careless run grades all three the same way:
  A. is BFD absent / licence-gated on this platform?        (it is NOT)
  B. is the RIP-to-BFD binding absent?                      (it IS)
  C. does BFD itself work here at all?                      (it DOES)
A verdict of UNSUPPORTED is only honest if B is proven while A and C are
DISPROVEN, so the log must carry a working BFD session beside the refusals.

