  Two things are already settled here:
  - `show bfd session` DOES NOT EXIST on this build; the verb is `show bfd peer`.
    Confirms the triage note. A tester who runs `show bfd session`, reads
    `% Invalid input` and grades BFD absent is wrong.
  - the BFD refusal carries NO licence clause ("% BFD protocol daemon is not
    running") while the RIP one does ("...or feature license is not available").
    So BFD on this platform is service-gated ONLY -- there is no BFD licence bit
    to be missing, which matches `show license` at triage.

