  Topology for the RIP part: DUT 10.0.61.1/30 <-> swi_b 10.0.61.2/30 on vlan61.
  Each device owns a loopback prefix the other can only reach through RIP.

    DUT (/dev/u2)                            swi_b (/dev/u3)
      interface lo                             interface lo
       ip address 192.168.80.1/24               ip address 192.168.70.1/24
      router rip                                ip address 192.168.71.1/24 secondary
       network 10.0.61.0/30                    router rip
       network 192.168.80.0/24                  network 10.0.61.0/30
                                                network 192.168.70.0/24
      [work/s3b-rip-u2.log]                    [work/s3c-rip-u3.log, s3d-lo2-u3.log]

  ** 192.168.71.0/24 was deliberately CONFIGURED on swi_b and NOT advertised. **
  It is the baseline-off subject: a prefix that exists and is connected on the
  neighbour, and is still unreachable because nothing advertises it. That makes
  the "off" measurement live inside the same capture as the "on" one.

  NOTE on the DUT's `lo`: `ip address 192.168.80.1/24 secondary` was REFUSED with
  `% Configure primary first lo` [work/s3-rip-u2.log], so the DUT's loopback took
  the address as its PRIMARY. swi_b's `lo` already had a primary, so its second
  address needed `secondary`. The two devices differ; do not copy one recipe to
  the other blind.

